Use MODE_BACKGROUND_ACTIVITY_START_ALLOW_IF_VISIBLE instead of
MODE_BACKGROUND_ACTIVITY_START_DENIED to allow legitimate foreground
usage of AddAccountSettings while blocking background exploits.
The previous fix (ag/40655215) broke the foreground use case (b/530008611)
because DENIED acts as a total opt-out for all BAL exemptions.
ALLOW_IF_VISIBLE enforces visibility checks but skips privileged UID
exemptions, thus blocking background bypasses while allowing normal
foreground usage.

Test with 3 authenticators: 1) BypassBAL POC (2) Google (3) Tiktok
Flows tested:
1. BypassBAL POC app when clicked launches MainActivity, but SecondActivity launch is blocked. In Settings, when BypassBAL authenticator is selected, Settings wait for 30 seconds then shows the SecondActivity.
2. Google and Tiktok open their login page when selected in Settings.
3. Google apps (Drive, Gmail) open login page through OneGoogle.

Bug: 313418699
Test: build
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
